Like Sudoku (aka "Magic Squares") hasn't been around forever, and isn't
just as boring if not possibly even more annoying?

Sokoban is a one-time thing; once solved, you always know the answer,
and it becomes boring because it's an exercise in boulder-pushing.

Sudoku is much the same; once you know the trick, it's an exercise in
minor mental gymnastics.  It takes fewer game turns, but is equally boring.

I've got it!  Remove Sokoban entirely, and simply put a bag of holding
or amulet of reflection where the stairs to Sokoban would have been.

